Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:05.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now the crowd law: on average,\Nenergy in equals energy out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.15,0:00:10.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Three ways to impose it,\Nat settings of {\c&H7AAF1B&}eta{\c&HF7F4F2&} never seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.08,0:00:15.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One: during training, the crowd\Nloss, with its two juries.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.90,0:00:18.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Against a control run of equal length,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.19,0:00:22.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}the {\c&H00A1ED&}distribution distance{\c&HF7F4F2&} drops from\Ntwo point five to zero point seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.10,0:00:25.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The control itself gains nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.20,0:00:30.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Two: after training,\Nreweight the generated crowd.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.85,0:00:33.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Where the model is worst,\Na poll of five hundred
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.05,0:00:37.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}shrinks to one person,\Nand the crowd gets worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.32,0:00:42.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Three: rescale every\Nsnapshot onto the budget.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.71,0:00:45.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Each snapshot now dissipates\Nthe same: a spike,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.93,0:00:48.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}under a thousandth of the true spread.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.18,0:00:54.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Yet the same {\c&H00A1ED&}distribution distance{\c&HF7F4F2&},\Nbuilt on spectra, improves: it is fooled.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.25,0:01:00.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Only the spread gives the spike away.\NThe crowd loss shows no spike.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.09,0:01:04.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One training seed each,\Ninterpolation only,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.20,0:01:07.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}every model far above the noise floor.
